From: Daniel Gabay <daniel.gabay@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:37:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: Verify frame length before reading auth_alg

In mlme_event(), auth_alg is read from mgmt->u.auth.auth_alg when
len >= 24, but this field starts at offset 24 and is 2 bytes wide,
requiring len >= 26. A management frame with exactly 24 bytes (header
only, no body) triggers a 2-byte OOB heap read. Guard the access with
a proper length check.

(Backported from hostap 8a2611102, adapted to the context of this
snapshot.)

Fixes: 58a96187eed8 ("nl80211: Allow PASN Authentication frames with random (foreign) MAC address")
Signed-off-by: Daniel Gabay <daniel.gabay@intel.com>
---
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211_event.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_event.c b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_event.c
index 515d904..6fd734a 100644
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_event.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_event.c
@@ -1832,7 +1832,9 @@ static void mlme_event(struct i802_bss *bss,
 	/* PASN Authentication frame can be received with a different source MAC
 	 * address. Allow NL80211_CMD_FRAME event with foreign addresses also.
 	 */
-	if (cmd == NL80211_CMD_FRAME && len >= 24) {
+	/* auth_alg is the 2 octets right after the 24-octet header */
+	if (cmd == NL80211_CMD_FRAME &&
+	    len >= IEEE80211_HDRLEN + 2) {
 		const struct ieee80211_mgmt *mgmt;
 		u16 fc;
 
